// Q-052 An address `public_only` refuses is reported as "Dns Failed: resolve dns name '127.0.0.1:9'", though nothing was looked up: an IP and its port, said as a failed name lookup
// mode: run
// open-when: Dns Failed: resolve dns name '127.0.0.1:9'
// fixed-when: public_only
// From FEEDBACK5.md (found on ae6a6e5). app/stays was pointed at a dead Overpass server to try its
// fallback; the log said "Dns Failed" for 127.0.0.1:9 and for 203.0.113.1 (a documentation
// address). The refusal itself is right (and instant): the words send one to check DNS. Saying that
// `public_only` refused a private address, and which, would point at the cause.

print(http.get("http://127.0.0.1:9/x", {}, { public_only: true }))
